# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (CI: TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=cmake/tsan.supp).
#
# Drogon and trantor come from distro packages that are not built with -fsanitize=thread, so TSan
# cannot see the atomics of trantor's lock-free task queue (EventLoop::queueInLoop) or the eventfd
# that wakes a loop. Our own hand-offs to a loop publish themselves with __tsan_release/acquire
# (queue_in_loop() in libs/common/src/http.cpp); what remains are the queue's internal nodes,
# allocated by the queueing thread and freed by the loop. Only reports with these trantor frames on
# a stack are suppressed: races in handlers, on worker threads or on the event loops still show.
race:trantor::EventLoop::queueInLoop
race:trantor::EventLoop::wakeup
